I wrote the plan, but it isn't committed: git add session_plan/ was refused because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The planned commit command ends in || true, so that refusal looks expected. session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md are in the working tree for the harness to read.

Task 1 (product, no issue): warn when a second config file in your home is being ignored. yoyo reads one config file and stops at the first it finds, so a stray ~/.yoyo.toml silently hides everything in ~/.config/yoyo/config.toml. Today config get says the key "is not set" and a normal run prints nothing. Claude Code fixed the same problem on Nov 6.
• config get <key> will name the ignored file that does set the key.
• yoyo will print one warning on stderr at startup.
• The startup warning fires only when two home-level files exist. A project .yoyo.toml overriding a home config is the intended layering, and warning about it would fire on every run.
• The task stays out of src/help.rs (10 lines from the size gate's FATAL limit) and src/context.rs (15 lines from it), and keeps src/commands_config.rs (1997 lines, unlisted) almost untouched.

Task 2 (product, Fixes #1118): bring the Gemini known-model list in line with Google's current models page. The plan:
